From f4808ec06b930efe595acd197038a0c7aeb41654 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "HT9045 Machine (V906)" <Claude_RDBC_02@honprec.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 08:03:40 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] 1203REOPEN-2: six fixes from the review of the re-open flow
 (hourly loop on 026dcd7 / c05c3bb / 012d4a9 / web 6ae80ab).

C1 (high) retries did not wait for the module check's verdict (it needs up to 10 s itself), so every try interrupted the previous one and the 3rd try raised WAR16157 one tick after it was issued -> EtherCAT/Pci1203Reopen.h: each attempt waits for a verdict (the fault reported again = failed, Recovered = done, none within 30 s = failed); the next try 10 s after a failure; the alarm only after the 3rd attempt's verdict.
C2 (mid-high) only kPass called Recovered -> kWriteIni / kWriteSkipped / kIniBad (no list to compare = no mismatch) also end a pending re-open (tools/wb_serve.cpp, three same-line hooks), avoiding extra whole-card re-opens and a false WAR16157.
C3 (mid) pci1203.ring.reset was a wire command with no stopped check (any client could reset ring 0 while running) -> no wire name; INTERNAL, audit name "(internal)"; only the re-open flow issues it.
C4 a build without HAVE_PCI1203 raised WAR16150 + WAR16157 at every boot -> "not linked" is not an open failure.
C5 a try that never reached the card still cleared fAllMotorHome and started a module-check generation -> AttemptNotIssued: counts as a failed try, no HOME lost, no new generation.
C6 the button could give 4 tries -> a fault during a manual re-open keeps the try count.

Tests: Pci1203Reopen 33/33 (verdict wait, no alarm before the 3rd verdict, 30 s timeout, manual keeps the count, not issued), Pci1203Pure 105/105; readonly / control gates PASS; code-after-comment scan 0. Plausible items not changed (reported): no wait between the reset and the re-scan; RescanRing does not rebuild IO widths / IO map; a whole-card re-open on the tick thread when the IO thread is not running; drives "missing" at boot before the safety circuit is reset. Debug + release (affected targets). WORKLOG section 2 row 145.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
