-    kCmdAxSetDriveHome, kCmdAxSetExtDrive, kCmdAxSetCmdPos, kCmdAxSetActPos, kCmdAxMoveHome, kCmdAxSetInitCfg, kCmdAxTorqueLimitSet, kCmdVc8DoSet, kCmdVc8SdoWriteI16, kCmdRingReset   /*AI(W906-1203REOPEN) 20261007: kCmdRingReset = value: ring mask 1 (ring 0) / 2 (ring 1) / 3; wire "pci1203.ring.reset"; Acm_MasResetRing per ring then a slave re-scan + axis re-open (TPci1203Monitor::RescanRing), falling back to the whole-card Rescan() when the export is missing or a reset fails. Appended LAST*/   //AI(W906-VACUNIT-1203) 20260930: + the ECAT-VC8 vacuum unit's two writes, INTERNAL (no wire name, audit name "(internal)"; only EtherCAT/Pci1203Vc8Route.inc issues them, for HW.VacuumUnit's golden buttons). kCmdVc8DoSet: port = the monitor DO slot, bit, value 0/1 -> Acm_DaqDoSetBitEx(dev, d.ring, d.station, d.stationChan*8+bit, v) -- refused unless the byte is ring-attributed and read back, the channel is 16..31 and the station passes the ECAT-VC8 identity check in OP (EtherCAT/Pci1203Vc8.h). kCmdVc8SdoWriteI16: vc8Slave = the monitor slave slot, vc8Vc 0..7, vc8Sub 02h (value exactly 1, threshold mode) or 13h (value 0..32767 = KpaToVC8), I16 DataSize 2 -> Acm_DevWriteSDOData(dev, v.ring, v.addr, 8000h+10h*vc, sub, ...) -- same station refusals. Not motion, not output-first. Appended LAST so no existing kind changes value.   //AI(W906-MT-FIX1) 20260926: kCmdAxTorqueLimitSet = INTERNAL (no wire name, audit name "(internal)"): axis = the 1203 monitor axis index, value = the torque limit in 0.1 % of rated (UINT16, whole number 0..65535). ONE Execute writes that value to 60E0h AND 60E1h (68E0h / 68E1h for a two-axis unit's B half), reads both back and compares; Pci1203CmdResult::ok / value / valueValid / failStep carry the verdict (see there). NO retry inside (the laptop's layer retries). Refused for no station / ambiguous station / unknown sub-axis / a station that is not CiA 402, like the monitor's 6077h read. Not motion, not output-first. Appended LAST so no existing kind cha